  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "DELTA and GESTEP read their second argument first",
  "statement": "When both arguments of DELTA or GESTEP are bad, the error comes from the second one: DELTA(TRUE,#REF!) is #REF! and DELTA(#REF!,TRUE) is #VALUE!. With two errors, DELTA gives the second. ERF reads left to right: ERF(TRUE,#REF!) is #VALUE! and ERF(#REF!,TRUE) is #REF!. A logical is rejected in either position of these functions, whether typed or held in a cell: DELTA(TRUE,0) and DELTA(2,TRUE) are #VALUE!, and DELTA(B1,0) with TRUE in B1 is #VALUE!, while an empty B1 reads as 0 and gives 1.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "16 recorded DELTA and GESTEP formula readings, 8 readings each with errors and text held in cells, and the ERF companions on the same sheets. GESTEP gave the same pattern as DELTA in every pair.",
  "inferred": null,
  "documentation": null,
